# Commands run by the launchd job com.hakios.demo (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.metalcompute).
#
# The first dispatch through Metal on this GPU. metal_props opens the two discovery properties,
# so MTLCreateSystemDefaultDevice() returns RedwoodMetalDevice (the sweep of test60 settled
# that), and metal_drv_test then:
#
#   - reads a system .metallib and asks the driver to compile a function from it, which is
#     libredwoodair's AIR front end feeding panfrost's Bifrost compiler;
#   - makes the buffers the kernel binds and dispatches it on the GPU;
#   - reads the buffer back and says whether the dispatch happened at all.
#
# MetalFaceMask_InitMinMax is the first one y2sios tried for the same reason: exactly one device
# buffer (24 bytes, read_write, atomicMinMax), no textures and no samplers, and it writes its
# buffer unconditionally -- so an all-zero result means the dispatch did not happen rather than
# that the kernel had nothing to say.
#
# say_run puts every line in the kernel log (a job's stdout is kept nowhere); if the test dies,
# the line after it still turns the properties off.
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 40
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props show
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props on
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_drv_test /System/Library/CoreImage/PortraitFilters.cifilter/default.metallib MetalFaceMask_InitMinMax
/redwood/bin/say_run /redwood/bin/metal_props off
